ng the lead from -20.1 to -12.2. Each Black push lost about as much as White's reply won back, so the lead stayed within a narrow band."}, {"turn": 32, "text": "The decisive move. White was ahead by 12.0, but C8 lost 14.0 points and moved the lead from -12.0 to +2.0, which put Black ahead. The engine's choice was A7, the point Black took next. After this the lead never returned to White."}, {"turn": 34, "text": "A8 lost another 5.5 points, taking the lead from +2.0 to +7.5. White had a chance to fight back after C8, but this move pushed Black's lead even further past the komi. GPT-6.1 Sol's total of 6 blunders for the game, each costing 6 points or more, shows how much was lost in a few moves."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "All code (inspect100, verify100, the play100 wrapper, log/SGF/markdown writing via apply_patch) only parses returned boards, counts groups/liberties/area, replays the already-played moves to check legality and captures, and saves records; none of it loops over candidate moves, ranks moves, or looks ahead. Every move was submitted manually by name through mcp__go__play.", "stop": false}}